{
  "dom_id": "step-q177589",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the line that has a slope of $\\frac{5}{2}$ and passes through the point $(6,7).$ What are the coordinates of the $y$-intercept?\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$",
  "worked_solution": "Given that $m=\\frac{5}{2}$, we substitute the coordinates of the given point into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =mx+b \\\\ (7) & =(\\frac{5}{2})(6)+b \\\\ 7 & =15+b \\\\ -8 & =b \\\\ b & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,-8).$",
